{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
  "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: GLENN W. RHODES, ESQ., San Francisco, Cal.; on behalf of the Petitioner. THEODORE S. ALLISON, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carlsbad Technology, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The single issue presented in this case is whether the bar to review under 1447(d) is applicable to a district court's discretionary decision to decline the exercise of supplemental jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Isn't there something odd about saying if it's really fundamental like the presence or absence of subject matter jurisdiction, that is not reviewable? It's not disputed, right? That if the district court says, I lack subject matter jurisdiction over, let's say, the RICO claim, as wrong as that might be, that would not be reviewable, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Theodore S. Allison (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me begin with Petitioner's counsel's last remark, and that is that we don't know what the consequences would be, except that we do know that by applying the review bar to supplemental jurisdiction remands, it would bring us closer to achieving the purpose that has been expressed in the statutes of Congress since 1887."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But that was a dissenting opinion, and that was how many years ago? How many years?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Glenn W. Rhodes",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, I would just like to reiterate that when Congress enacted 1367, that gave it Article III jurisdiction in those matters, just as 1331 and 1332 do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Glenn W. Rhodes",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would also like to reiterate that -- that stare decisis should be maintained over this statutory interpretation because it has proved to be workable rather than not workable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Glenn W. Rhodes",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Again, the circuit courts -- even though as Mr. Chief Justice has iterated that they have to follow this, they have found it to be a workable framework."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Glenn W. Rhodes",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, again, as the Court expressed in Powerex, they agreed that in Quackenbush that Thermtron was not altered. And Congress has -- has seemingly ratified this Court's interpretation in Thermtron, and it has been applied in Quackenbush."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it's a huge State claim and a tiny Federal claim, why wouldn't that properly be regarded as an absence of jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Glenn W. Rhodes",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My response to that, Mr. Chief Justice, is that until a court decides that it was an abuse of discretion, the district court had jurisdiction under 1367(c) to either exercise that power or not exercise that power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e60f9e1e64184f8eddbb4ed1424785b595fcd4bcfcd413ab1eeff545c1ae1bc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e60f9e1e6418-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
